@startuml
!include opk-style.puml

title Open Perception Kit Container Component Overview

top to bottom direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam ranksep 80
skinparam nodesep 70
skinparam linetype ortho

component "External application /\nservice" as External
interface "FrameResults packet" as IPerception

rectangle "Open Perception Kit Container" {
  package "Open Perception Kit element chain" as CHAIN {
    component "opkinfer" as OPKINFER
    component "opktracker" as OPKTRACKER
    component "opkperformance" as OPKPERF
    component "opkosd" as OPKOSD
    component "opksink" as OPKSINK
  }

  package "Inference execution inside opkinfer" as INFERBOX {
    component "OpChain / Op system\n(JSON descriptors,\nconfigure -> bind -> process,\nloopId-based execution)" as OPC
    component "Preprocess Ops" as PRE
    component "Inference Ops\n(ONNX / ExecuTorch)" as INF
    component "Postprocess Parsers" as POST
  }

  package "Stable runtime contract" as CONTRACT {
    component "FrameResultsMeta /\nFrameResults" as PERC
    component "Generated packet serializer /\npublisher boundary" as PERCSER
  }

  package "Current pipeline host layer" as HOST {
    component "GStreamer runtime\n(current media transport,\nscheduling, and metadata carrier)" as GST
  }
}

OPKINFER -down-> OPKTRACKER
OPKTRACKER -down-> OPKPERF
OPKPERF -down-> OPKOSD
OPKOSD -down-> OPKSINK

OPC -down-> PRE
PRE -down-> INF
INF -down-> POST
OPC ..> OPKINFER : executes inside

CHAIN --> PERC

PERC -down-> PERCSER
PERCSER -down-> IPerception
IPerception -down-> External

GST -up-> CHAIN

INFERBOX -[hidden]right-> CHAIN
CHAIN -[hidden]right-> CONTRACT
CHAIN -[hidden]down-> HOST
INFERBOX -[hidden]down-> HOST
CONTRACT -[hidden]down-> HOST
CONTRACT -[hidden]down-> IPerception
IPerception -[hidden]down-> External

legend bottom
- GStreamer is the current pipeline/orchestration host layer.
  It handles media transport, scheduling, and metadata carriage.
- OpChain is the inference-specific glue inside opkinfer.
  It binds preprocess, backend execution, and postprocess stages.
- FrameResults is the generated runtime contract passed between Open Perception Kit components
  and published to external applications.
- opkinfer creates and enriches that contract via OpChain execution.
- opktracker and opkperformance append more structured runtime data.
- opkosd and opksink consume it for rendering and publication.
endlegend

@enduml
